Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.

ABOUT THE TEAM

The Anduril Imaging team develops state-of-the-art imaging systems across both hardware and software, deployed to tackle the most significant security challenges of America and its allies. The team is heavily involved in utilizing computer vision, perception, electro-optical, infrared, and sensor data to give the US and its allies an advantage.

ABOUT THE JOB

As a member of the Supply Chain Team, you will&nbsp;be responsible for&nbsp;managing supplier relationships, negotiating prices, and ensuring parts are delivered on time. This is an exciting opportunity to be apart a growing and dynamic team working closely with engineering and manufacturing teams to support the development and sourcing of&nbsp;cutting-edge&nbsp;defense technologies.&nbsp;The right person for this role is someone who can excel in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment where small teams share a broad variety of duties; has strong people and communication skills; is eager to identify opportunities, find solutions, execute plans, and evaluate results critically and expediently; is committed to learning from mistakes and driven to improve and enhance performance of oneself, others, and the company. &nbsp;

WHAT YOU'LL DO &nbsp;

• Own procurement process cradle-to-grave for multiple product lines or commodity types &nbsp;

• Lead cross-functional projects to achieve cost, quality, and delivery targets&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Maintain procurement master data across&nbsp;multiple&nbsp;Bill of Materials to ensure&nbsp;accurate&nbsp;information is flowed to Planning and&nbsp;Production&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Support&nbsp;Sourcing&nbsp;Engineering&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Manufacturing&nbsp;teams&nbsp;to&nbsp;determine&nbsp;best sources&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Identify&nbsp;and execute cost reduction projects; including strategic procurement&nbsp;and&nbsp;commercial&nbsp;term negotiation &nbsp;

• Onboard new suppliers&nbsp;in accordance with&nbsp;Anduril Quality Manual and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;the Approved Supplier List&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Evaluate suppliers using procurement KPIs and analyze performance trends as part of the Supply Chain performance reviews &nbsp;

• Conduct research, benchmark, and collect market data to ensure a best-in-class supply base &nbsp;

• Place purchase orders and resolve downstream issues with receiving, finance, and accounting &nbsp;

REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp; &nbsp;

• 5+ years of Procurement or Supply Chain Management experience &nbsp;

• A bachelors degree or equivalent experience

• Experience with ERP and PLM systems &nbsp;

• Experience with technical procurement &nbsp;

• Effective written, verbal, and presentation skills &nbsp;

• Exceptional analytical and organizational skills &nbsp;

• Eligible to obtain and maintain an active U.S. Secret security clearance

PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp;

• Experience in relevant manufacturing industries (e.g., Aerospace and Defense, Automotive, Space, Electronics) &nbsp;

• FAR/DFARS experience &nbsp;

US Salary Range
$99,000 &mdash; $130,000 USD

